\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Earlier single-volume experiments (Sim2 only; single volume, single seed). In S2b the fresh-noise test error was lowest after about 500 steps and then rose while the training error kept falling: the network memorised one brain. Training only on simulated noise (never seeing the real $\psi $) gave the same behaviour, so the real noise realisation is not the cause; the likely cause is the lack of anatomical diversity (not proven).}}{15}{table.caption.30}\protected@file@percent }
